From: Banks Troutman <banks.troutman@oxos.com>
Date: Wed, 20 May 2026 12:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] PlatformBootManagerLib: suppress UEFI splash phase

The L4T R35 UEFI BDS PlatformBootManagerAfterConsole runs three
cosmetic / probe blocks before BdsWait:

  - BootLogoEnableLogo() paints the splash bitmap and emits ANSI
    cursor sequences to the serial ConOut.
  - DisplaySystemAndHotkeyInformation() reprints the firmware banner
    and the ESC/F11/Enter hotkey hints to GOP and to serial.
  - MemoryTest() locates two protocols and runs an outer TestModes
    loop even when every *Enabled flag in PcdMemoryTest is FALSE.

On a headless Xavier NX A203 the user-visible "splash" between
NvDisp-Init failing (no HDMI) and L4TLauncher firing is dominated by
these blocks. Disable all three. ConOut still produces serial text
output for L4TLauncher and the kernel EFI stub. BdsWait countdown is
already skipped via the Timeout EFI variable (=0). BootOrder
enumeration and the L4TLauncher boot path are untouched.

Signed-off-by: Banks Troutman <banks.troutman@oxos.com>
---
--- a/Silicon/NVIDIA/Library/PlatformBootManagerLib/PlatformBm.c
+++ b/Silicon/NVIDIA/Library/PlatformBootManagerLib/PlatformBm.c
@@ -1757,21 +1757,24 @@
   )
 {
   //
-  // Show the splash screen.
+  // Banks: suppress splash. BootLogoEnableLogo() blits the splash bitmap to
+  // the GOP and emits ANSI cursor sequences to serial ConOut.
   //
-  BootLogoEnableLogo ();
+  // BootLogoEnableLogo ();
 
   if (!IsSingleBootNeeded ()) {
     //
-    // Display system and hotkey information after console is ready.
+    // Banks: suppress the firmware banner + ESC/F11/Enter hotkey reprint.
+    // This is the visible "splash text" on the serial console.
     //
-    DisplaySystemAndHotkeyInformation ();
+    // DisplaySystemAndHotkeyInformation ();
   }
 
   //
-  // Run memory test
+  // Banks: skip memory test entirely. Even when every *Enabled flag in
+  // PcdMemoryTest is FALSE the protocol locate + outer loop still runs.
   //
-  MemoryTest ();
+  // MemoryTest ();
 
   // Ipmi communication
   PrintBmcIpAddresses ();
--
